{"type":"message","id":"998b19ba","parentId":"41793c93","timestamp":"2026-02-27T03:42:27.816Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Gateway is running. Now I need to figure out how to send a task to the design-agent. Let me check if there's a tool or API to do that. Looking at the task description, it mentions using @design-agent, @code-agent, etc. which suggests some mention-based system.\n\nLet me try to find if there's a way to start a new session with a specific agent. Looking at the task description again:\n\n\"### 1. 设计阶段 (@design-agent)\"\n\nThis mentions @design-agent which might be a way to call another agent. Let me try a simpler approach - since I don't have direct access to spawn subagents, let me do the design work myself and then coordinate with code-agent.\n\nActually wait - I need to re-read my role. Looking at the context:\n- I'm a \"subagent spawned by the main agent\"\n- My role is to \"handle: 阅读 search-agent 的调研报告，组织 fsrs-memory 项目重构\"\n\nSo I'm supposed to organize the refactoring. Looking at how subagents were used in the past (from the memory file), they seem to work through some messaging system. Let me see if I can find out how this works by checking if there's an API endpoint or tool.\n\nActually, looking at the tools available to me - I don't see a \"sessions_send\" tool. But looking at the previous conversation logs, it seems like the main agent used some kind of tool to spawn subagents. Perhaps I should just do the work myself in a more limited fashion, or I need to figure out the right command.\n\nLet me try using exec to find out if there's an OpenClaw command to start a subagent session.","thinkingSignature":"578fb4f1d5bd405f0afc573bf5a7fdd1f755f797cac9e1dda8b321f17012ff60"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9fz145o0tfvl_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent && npx openclaw --help 2>&1 | grep -i task"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minima