{"type":"message","id":"af7cfc75","parentId":"0e825cf4","timestamp":"2026-02-27T03:42:38.123Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, that doesn't help. Let me try a different approach. Since I can't seem to spawn subagents directly, let me proceed with doing the design work myself. I'll analyze the project and create the architecture document, then try to coordinate the implementation.\n\nActually, wait - let me re-read the tools more carefully. I see \"message\" tool is available, which is described as \"Send, delete, and manage messages via channel plugins\". Maybe I can use this to send a message to another agent? But the description says \"channel plugins\", not agents.\n\nLet me try a simpler approach: since the task is complex and involves multiple phases, let me first create a comprehensive design document myself, then I'll figure out how to coordinate the rest.\n\nActually, I think the issue is that I'm a subagent and I need to communicate back to the main agent who will then spawn other subagents. Let me re-read my instructions:\n\n\"Complete this task. That's your entire purpose.\"\n\"When complete, your final response should include...\"\n\nSo I should complete this task myself. But then it also says:\n\"- 你被创建来处理: 阅读 search-agent 的调研报告，组织 fsrs-memory 项目重构\"\n\nWhich means I need to organize the refactoring. Let me see if I can at least do the design phase myself and then send results back.\n\nActually, wait - I think I'm overthinking this. Let me just proceed with the design phase by doing it myself. I'll:\n1. Analyze the current code\n2. Identify bugs\n3. Create an architecture document\n4. Then figure out how to proceed with implementation\n\nLet me start by doing a thorough analysis of the current codebase.","thinkingSignature":"1b7bc0bc78f1734c947a3aeea2402ac37d028ee540099b5d9813b432bc672ef9"},{"type":"text","text":"由于工具限制，我将直接进行设计分析并创建架构文档。让我先全面分析当前项目的代码：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xm0a6880zzen_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/web/server.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":16483,"output":398,"cacheRead":7930,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24811,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772163749384}}
{"type":"message","id":"1f722d15","parentId":"af7cfc75","timestamp":"2026-02-27T03:42:38.147Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_xm0a6880zzen_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// server.js - Express Backend for FSRS Web UI with Multi-deck & Theme support\nconst express = require('express');\nconst cors = require('cors');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\n\nconst app = express();\nconst PORT = process.env.PORT || 3001;\n\n// Middleware\napp.use(cors());\napp.use(express.json());\napp.use(express.static(path.join(__dirname, 'public')));\n\n// Database setup - connect to existing cards.db\nconst DB_PATH = process.env.DB_PATH || path.join(__dirname, '..', 'data', 'cards.db');\nconst db = new Database(DB_PATH);\n\n// Import FSRS engine\nconst FSRSEngine = require('../src/fsrs');\n\n// ==================== Database Helper Functions ====================\n\n// Fix inconsistent state values in database\nfunction fixCardStates() {\n  try {\n    // Fix \"2.0\" state to \"review\" (this was a bug where State.Review = 2 was stored as string)\n    const result = db.prepare(\"UPDATE cards SET state = 'review' WHERE state = '2.0'\").run();\n    if (result.changes > 0) {\n      console.log(`Fixed ${result.changes} cards with invalid state '2.0'`);\n    }\n    \n    // Fix empty or null states to \"new\"\n    db.prepare(\"UPDATE cards SET state = 'new' WHERE state IS NULL OR state = ''\").run();\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Error fixing card states:', error);\n  }\n}\n\n// Run state fix on startup\nfixCardStates();\n\n// Get current local time for database queries\nfunction getLocalNow() {\n  return new Date().toISOString();\n}\n\n// ==================== Settings API ====================\n\n// Get theme\napp.get('/api/settings/theme', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const theme = db.prepare(\"SELECT value FROM settings WHERE key = 'theme'\").get();\n    res.json({ success: true, data: theme ? theme.value : 'light' });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Set theme\napp.post('/api/settings/theme', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { theme } = req.body;\n    if (!theme || !['light', 'dark'].includes(theme)) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Invalid theme' });\n    }\n    db.prepare(`\n      INSERT INTO settings (key, value) VALUES ('theme', ?)\n      ON CONFLICT(key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value\n    `).run(theme);\n    res.json({ success: true, data: theme });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// ==================== Deck API ====================\n\n// Get all decks\napp.get('/api/decks', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    // Use localtime for due_date comparison to match user timezone\n    const decks = db.prepare(`\n      SELECT d.*, \n        (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cards WHERE deck_id = d.id) as card_count,\n        (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cards WHERE deck_id = d.id AND strftime('%s', due_date) <= strftime('%s', 'now')) as due_count\n      FROM decks d \n      ORDER BY d.id ASC\n    `).all();\n    res.json({ success: true, data: decks });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Get single deck\napp.get('/api/decks/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const deck = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM decks WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    if (!deck) {\n      return res.status(404).json({ success: false, error: 'Deck not found' });\n    }\n    res.json({ success: true, data: deck });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Create deck\napp.post('/api/decks', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { name, description } = req.body;\n    if (!name) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Deck name required' });\n    }\n    \n    const stmt = db.prepare('INSERT INTO decks (name, description) VALUES (?, ?)');\n    const result = stmt.run(name, description || '');\n    \n    const newDeck = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM decks WHERE id = ?').get(result.lastInsertRowid);\n    res.json({ success: true, data: newDeck });\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error.message.includes('UNIQUE')) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Deck name already exists' });\n    }\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Update deck\napp.put('/api/decks/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { name, description } = req.body;\n    const deckId = parseInt(req.params.id);\n    \n    if (deckId === 1) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Cannot modify default deck' });\n    }\n    \n    db.prepare(`\n      UPDATE decks SET name = ?, description = ?, updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = ?\n    `).run(name, description || '', deckId);\n    \n    const updatedDeck = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM decks WHERE id = ?').get(deckId);\n    res.json({ success: true, data: updatedDeck });\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error.message.includes('UNIQUE')) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Deck name already exists' });\n    }\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Delete deck\napp.delete('/api/decks/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const deckId = parseInt(req.params.id);\n    \n    if (deckId === 1) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Cannot delete default deck' });\n    }\n    \n    // Move cards to default deck before deleting\n    db.prepare('UPDATE cards SET deck_id = 1 WHERE deck_id = ?').run(deckId);\n    db.prepare('DELETE FROM decks WHERE id = ?').run(deckId);\n    \n    res.json({ success: true });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// ==================== Card API ====================\n\n// Get all cards (with optional deck filter)\napp.get('/api/cards', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const deckId = req.query.deck ? parseInt(req.query.deck) : null;\n    let cards;\n    if (deckId) {\n      cards = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ? ORDER BY created_at DESC').all(deckId);\n    } else {\n      cards = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards ORDER BY created_at DESC').all();\n    }\n    res.json({ success: true, data: cards });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Get due cards (with optional deck filter)\napp.get('/api/cards/due', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const deckId = req.query.deck ? parseInt(req.query.deck) : null;\n    // Use localtime for consistency with deck stats\n    const now = new Date();\n    let cards;\n    if (deckId) {\n      cards = db.prepare(`\n        SELECT * FROM cards \n        WHERE deck_id = ? AND strftime('%s', due_date) <= strftime('%s', 'now')\n        ORDER BY due_date ASC\n      `).all(deckId);\n    } else {\n      cards = db.prepare(`\n        SELECT * FROM cards \n        WHERE strftime('%s', due_date) <= strftime('%s', 'now')\n        ORDER BY due_date ASC\n      `).all();\n    }\n    res.json({ success: true, data: cards });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Get single card\napp.get('/api/cards/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const card = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    if (!card) {\n      return res.status(404).json({ success: false, error: 'Card not found' });\n    }\n    res.json({ success: true, data: card });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Add new card (with optional deck)\napp.post('/api/cards', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { question, answer, deck_id } = req.body;\n    if (!question || !answer) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Question and answer required' });\n    }\n    \n    const deckId = deck_id ? parseInt(deck_id) : 1;\n    const now = new Date();\n    const stmt = db.prepare(`\n      INSERT INTO cards (deck_id, question, answer, due_date, created_at, state)\n      VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, 'new')\n    `);\n    const result = stmt.run(deckId, question, answer, now.toISOString(), now.toISOString());\n    \n    const newCard = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(result.lastInsertRowid);\n    res.json({ success: true, data: newCard });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Move card to different deck\napp.put('/api/cards/:id/deck', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { deck_id } = req.body;\n    db.prepare('UPDATE cards SET deck_id = ? WHERE id = ?').run(deck_id, req.params.id);\n    const updatedCard = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    res.json({ success: true, data: updatedCard });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Update card (after review)\napp.put('/api/cards/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { due_date, interval, ease_factor, repetitions, lapses, state, last_review } = req.body;\n    const stmt = db.prepare(`\n      UPDATE cards SET\n        due_date = ?,\n        interval = ?,\n        ease_factor = ?,\n        repetitions = ?,\n        lapses = ?,\n        state = ?,\n        last_review = ?\n      WHERE id = ?\n    `);\n    stmt.run(due_date, interval, ease_factor, repetitions, lapses, state, last_review, req.params.id);\n    \n    const updatedCard = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    res.json({ success: true, data: updatedCard });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Delete card\napp.delete('/api/cards/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    db.prepare('DELETE FROM cards WHERE id = ?').run(req.params.id);\n    res.json({ success: true });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// ==================== Statistics API ====================\n\n// Get statistics (with optional deck filter)\napp.get('/api/stats', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const deckId = req.query.deck ? parseInt(req.query.deck) : null;\n    \n    let total, due, reviewed, newCards, learning, avgEase;\n    \n    if (deckId) {\n      total = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ?').get(deckId).count;\n      due = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ? AND strftime('%s', due_date) <= strftime('%s', 'now')\").get(deckId).count;\n      reviewed = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ? AND repetitions > 0').get(deckId).count;\n      // Fixed: Added parentheses around OR condition and handle both 'new' state and repetitions = 0\n      newCards = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ? AND (state = 'new' OR repetitions = 0)\").get(deckId).count;\n      learning = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ? AND (state = 'learning' OR state = 'relearning')\").get(deckId).count;\n      avgEase = db.prepare('SELECT AVG(ease_factor) as avg FROM cards WHERE deck_id = ? AND repetitions > 0').get(deckId).avg || 2.5;\n    } else {\n      total = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards').get().count;\n      due = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE strftime('%s', due_date) <= strftime('%s', 'now')\").get().count;\n      reviewed = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE repetitions > 0').get().count;\n      // Fixed: Added parentheses around OR condition\n      newCards = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE state = 'new' OR repetitions = 0\").get().count;\n      learning = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM cards WHERE state = 'learning' OR state = 'relearning'\").get().count;\n      avgEase = db.prepare('SELECT AVG(ease_factor) as avg FROM cards WHERE repetitions > 0').get().avg || 2.5;\n    }\n    \n    res.json({\n      success: true,\n      data: {\n        total,\n        due,\n        reviewed,\n        new: newCards,\n        learning,\n        avgEase: Math.round(avgEase * 100) / 100\n      }\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// ==================== Review API ====================\n\n// Preview intervals before rating\napp.get('/api/review/:id/preview', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const card = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    if (!card) {\n      return res.status(404).json({ success: false, error: 'Card not found' });\n    }\n    \n    const previews = {};\n    for (let rating = 1; rating <= 5; rating++) {\n      const result = FSRSEngine.previewIntervals(card, rating);\n      if (result) {\n        previews[rating] = formatInterval(result.interval);\n      }\n    }\n    \n    res.json({ success: true, data: previews });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Review card with FSRS rating\napp.post('/api/review/:id', (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const { rating } = req.body;\n    if (!rating || rating < 1 || rating > 5) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ success: false, error: 'Rating must be 1-5' });\n    }\n    \n    const card = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    if (!card) {\n      return res.status(404).json({ success: false, error: 'Card not found' });\n    }\n    \n    // Use FSRS engine for scheduling\n    const fsrsCard = FSRSEngine.dbToCard(card);\n    const result = FSRSEngine.repeat(fsrsCard, rating);\n    \n    if (!result) {\n      return res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: 'Failed to calculate FSRS' });\n    }\n    \n    // Update card\n    const now = new Date();\n    db.prepare(`\n      UPDATE cards SET\n        due_date = ?,\n        interval = ?,\n        ease_factor = ?,\n        repetitions = ?,\n        lapses = ?,\n        state = ?,\n        last_review = ?\n      WHERE id = ?\n    `).run(\n      result.due_date,\n      result.interval,\n      result.ease_factor,\n      result.repetitions,\n      result.lapses,\n      result.state,\n      now.toISOString(),\n      req.params.id\n    );\n    \n    const updatedCard = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = ?').get(req.params.id);\n    res.json({ \n      success: true, \n      data: updatedCard, \n      nextInterval: formatInterval(result.interval)\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// Helper function to format interval - properly handles minutes\nfunction formatInterval(days) {\n  if (days < 1) {\n    // Convert to minutes (days * 24 * 60)\n    const minutes = Math.round(days * 24 * 60);\n    if (minutes < 60) {\n      return `${minutes}m`;\n    } else {\n      // If more than 60 minutes, show hours\n      return `${Math.round(minutes / 60)}h`;\n    }\n  } else if (days < 30) {\n    return `${Math.round(days)}d`;\n  } else if (days < 365) {\n    return `${Math.round(days / 30)}mo`;\n  } else {\n    return `${Math.round(days / 365)}y`;\n  }\n}\n\n// Serve SPA for all other routes\napp.get('*', (req, res) => {\n  res.sendFile(path.join(__dirname, 'public', 'index.html'));\n});\n\n// Start server\napp.listen(PORT, () => {\n  console.log(`FSRS Web UI server running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);\n});\n\nmodule.exports = app;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772163758143}}
{"type":"message","id":"b363b4e0","parentId":"1f722d15","timestamp":"2026-02-27T03:42:42.515Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the server code. Let me also check the frontend app.js to understand the current UI implementation.","thinkingSignature":"ea9193b0cad6311645dd1aab342a73c28d128daf2782758ddeb0af9dc23ed712"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dvi4h1rhmhol_1","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":150,"path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/web/public/app.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":20844,"output":78,"cacheRead":7930,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28852,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772163758147}}
{"type":"message","id":"cdb1fc11","parentId":"b363b4e0","timestamp":"2026-02-27T03:42:42.534Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_dvi4h1rhmhol_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// FSRS Memory Web UI - Application Logic with Multi-deck & Theme support\n\nconst API_BASE = window.location.origin;\n\n// State\nlet currentView = 'study';\nlet currentDeckId = null;\nlet dueCards = [];\nlet allCards = [];\nlet allDecks = [];\nlet currentCardIndex = 0;\nlet currentCard = null;\nlet isAnswerShown = false;\nlet currentTheme = 'light';\n\n// ==================== Initialization ====================\n\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n  initTheme();\n  initNavigation();\n  initKeyboardShortcuts();\n  loadDecks();\n  loadStats();\n  loadDueCards();\n});\n\n// ==================== Theme ====================\n\nasync function initTheme() {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/settings/theme`);\n    const result = await response.json();\n    if (result.success) {\n      currentTheme = result.data || 'light';\n      applyTheme(currentTheme);\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to load theme:', error);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction applyTheme(theme) {\n  document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);\n  document.getElementById('theme-icon').textContent = theme === 'dark' ? '☀️' : '🌙';\n  currentTheme = theme;\n}\n\nasync function toggleTheme() {\n  const newTheme = currentTheme === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light';\n  try {\n    await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/settings/theme`, {\n      method: 'POST',\n      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify({ theme: newTheme })\n    });\n    applyTheme(newTheme);\n    showToast(`已切换到${newTheme === 'dark' ? '暗色' : '亮色'}主题`, 'success');\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to save theme:', error);\n    showToast('主题切换失败', 'error');\n  }\n}\n\n// ==================== Navigation ====================\n\nfunction initNavigation() {\n  const navItems = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item');\n  navItems.forEach(item => {\n    item.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      const view = item.dataset.view;\n      showView(view);\n    });\n  });\n}\n\nfunction showView(view) {\n  // Update nav\n  document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item').forEach(item => {\n    item.classList.toggle('active', item.dataset.view === view);\n  });\n  \n  // Update view\n  document.querySelectorAll('.view').forEach(v => {\n    v.classList.toggle('active', v.id === `${view}-view`);\n  });\n  \n  currentView = view;\n  \n  // Load data for specific views\n  if (view === 'study') {\n    loadDueCards();\n  } else if (view === 'cards') {\n    loadAllCards();\n  } else if (view === 'decks') {\n    loadDecksGrid();\n  } else if (view === 'stats') {\n    loadStats();\n  }\n}\n\n// ==================== Deck Management ====================\n\nasync function loadDecks() {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/decks`);\n    const result = await response.json();\n    \n    if (result.success) {\n      allDecks = result.data;\n      updateDeckSelectors();\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to load decks:', error);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction updateDeckSelectors() {\n  // Update sidebar deck selector\n  const sidebarSelect = document.getElementById('deck-select');\n  const addViewSelect = document.getElementById('deck-select-add');\n  \n  const options = allDecks.map(deck => \n    `<option value=\"${deck.id}\">${deck.name} (${deck.due_count || 0} 待复习)</option>`\n  ).join('');\n  \n  sidebarSelect.innerHTML = '<option value=\"\">全部牌组</option>' + options;\n  addViewSelect.innerHTML = options;\n  \n  // Set default selection\n  if (allDecks.length > 0 && !currentDeckId) {\n    addViewSelect.value = allDecks[0].id;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function changeDeck(deckId) {\n  currentDeckId = deckId ? parseInt(deckId) : null;\n  \n  // Update deck info in study view\n  const deckInfo = document.getElementById('deck-info');\n  if (currentDeckId) {\n    const deck = allDecks.find(d => d.id === currentDeckId);\n    deckInfo.textContent = `当前牌组: ${deck ? deck.name : ''}`;\n  } else {\n    deckInfo.textContent = '';\n  }\n  \n  // Reload data\n  if (currentView === 'study') {\n    loadDueCards();\n  } else if (currentView === 'cards') {\n\n[727 more lines in file. Use offset=151 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772163762531}}
